ides Trio, a specialty fertilizer that delivers potassium, sulfate, and magnesium in a single particle; salt for various markets, including animal feed, industrial applications, pool salt, and the treatment of roads and walkways for ice melting or to manage road conditions; magnesium chloride for use as a road treatment agent for deicing and dedusting; brines for use in oil and gas industry to support well workover and completion activities; and metal recovery salts. The company was founded in 2000 and is based in Denver, Colorado.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kevin S. Crutchfield | CEO & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 478 people. Revenue per employee of $624K ranks in the below the sector median among Basic Materials peers. Each employee generates $53K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Intrepid Potash, Inc is a small-cap basic materials business with a $440M market cap on $298M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 18% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $26M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.99\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 46\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 19% 